The endless blue sky I looked up at stretched on forever

27
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:04,240
The endless blue sky I looked up at stretched on forever

28
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:10,160
This winding and random road

29
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:10,160
This winding and random road

30
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:18,750
Is a map for our endless dreams

31
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:18,750
Is a map for our endless dreams

32
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:24,510
Even if hope misses its target

33
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:24,510
Even if hope misses its target

34
00:02:24,510 --> 00:02:33,270
As long as I get back up, my dreams will never end

35
00:02:24,510 --> 00:02:33,270
As long as I get back up, my dreams will never end

36
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:38,820
Number one! Get out in front, ahead of everyone

37
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:38,820
Number one! Get out in front, ahead of everyone

38
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:44,740
Start running, with your tricky play, towards the world stage! Start! Dash!

39
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:44,740
Start running, with your tricky play, towards the world stage! Start! Dash!

40
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:46,410
Run & Run!

41
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:46,410
Run & Run!

42
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:53,620
Only our aspirations are the signals that move us, bit by bit

43
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:53,620
Only our aspirations are the signals that move us, bit by bit

44
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:56,630
Blaze, blaze, blaze and launch the kick

45
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:56,630
Blaze, blaze, blaze and launch the kick

46
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:01,050
Jump out onto the huge TV screen

47
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:01,050
Jump out onto the huge TV screen

48
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:20,140
You're always getting up late. At this rate, you'll get completely lazy.

49
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:21,950
No way...

50
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:29,390
Go wash your face. Spring break ends today.

51
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:31,430
You're going to school tomorrow.

52
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:33,900
Oh right, school!

53
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:35,950
How did it go, Mom?

54
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:39,440
The formalities were a bit difficult, you see.

55
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:45,040
You were thinking of going to Shutetsu Elementary, but then suddenly you wanted to go to Nankatsu Elementary.

56
00:03:46,130 --> 00:03:48,450
I have to go to Nankatsu Elementary.

57
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:51,660
I'll accept your challenge at the interschool tournament!

58
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:57,550
But with you on the team, we'll definitely put on a great show against Shutetsu!

59
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:59,050
I made a promise, after all.

60
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,020
Mom.

61
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:01,840
Yes?

62
00:04:02,350 --> 00:04:05,370
It's a good thing we moved to this city.

63
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:10,890
Is that so? Then there's someone I want you to meet, Tsubasa.

64
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:13,270
Here, come inside.

65
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,150
Roberto Hongo!

66
00:04:19,150 --> 00:04:20,820
Hey. Good morning.

67
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:23,680
Why? Why? Why? Why?

68
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,320
Here, Tsubasa.

69
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,900
From your father.

70
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,330
Roberto brought it with him.

71
00:04:30,330 --> 00:04:32,050
From my dad?

72
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:37,260
Dear Tsubasa,

73
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:42,880
Roberto Hongo-san is a wonderful professional footballer...

74
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:46,470
...who played forward on the Brazilian national team.

75
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:50,630
Due to various reasons, he decided to come to Japan.

76
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:54,350
I asked him to live at our house.

77
00:04:55,490 --> 00:05:00,990
Tsubasa, I also told Roberto-san about you.

78
00:05:00,990 --> 00:05:04,910
While you can, learn football to your heart's content.

79
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:08,450
I'll be coming home soon.

80
00:05:08,450 --> 00:05:13,660
Awesome! Roberto Hongo is going to live with us! Awesome!

81
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,040
What?

82
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:17,060
But when did you get here?

83
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:24,830
Your mother mistook me for a burglar.

84
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:25,940
What?

85
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,340
She suddenly threw water over me.

86
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:31,420
But he arrived at 2 in the morning.

87
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,600
Two?!

88
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:36,600
You should have shown the letter right away too, Roberto.

89
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:37,430
Oh, come on...

90
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,110
Sorry.

91
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:42,240
Will you practice this afternoon?

92
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,280
Yes!

93
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:46,610
Today, Ishizaki-kun is going to introduce me to the soccer team.

94
00:05:46,610 --> 00:05:48,110
I see.

95
00:05:48,110 --> 00:05:51,580
Alright. In that case, you'll be getting a present from me.

96
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,660
Huh? A present?

97
00:05:57,110 --> 00:05:59,580
There's no way Wakabayashi lost.

98
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:01,600
I don't believe it.

99
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:05,930
How could Shutetsu's team lose to a single player?

100
00:06:05,930 --> 00:06:08,720
Even if it was against the B team, they're still a team that won the nationals.

101
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,300
I'm telling you, it's true!

102
00:06:10,930 --> 00:06:13,430
A truly amazing player!

103
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:16,000
And he dribbles the ball everywhere he goes!

104
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,030
Wait, are you talking about him?

105
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:28,110
Hey, Tsubasa!

106
00:06:28,110 --> 00:06:29,030
Ishizaki-kun!

107
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:33,330
Tsubasa, we've been waiting for you!

108
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:36,580
Here!

109
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,730
Nice move.

110
00:06:44,730 --> 00:06:45,770
Ishizaki-kun!

111
00:06:45,770 --> 00:06:46,590
What?

112
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:47,470
Here.

113
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:49,230
On me.

114
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,810
Is everything okay?

115
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:57,870
Okay, okay.

116
00:06:57,870 --> 00:06:59,730
Huh? Where's Roberto?

117
00:06:59,730 --> 00:07:01,190
He said he had something to do.

118
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:04,440
Is everyone from the soccer club?

119
00:07:07,390 --> 00:07:09,580
They might all look good, but they're not.

120
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:10,610
They might all look good, but they're not.

121
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:14,140
You're one to talk, Ishizaki?!

122
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,100
You couldn't even control it just now!

123
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:18,620
So what?! Now open your ears!

124
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:23,500
This is Ozora Tsubasa, who took back the soccer field!

125
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:24,630
Nice to meet you.

126
00:07:24,630 --> 00:07:26,010
Nice to meet you.

127
00:07:26,010 --> 00:07:29,340
Thank you very much for taking this place back.

128
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:33,370
I would have liked to see Wakabayashi concede a goal.

129
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,900
I would have liked to see it too.

130
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:36,790
By the way...

131
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:41,440
...will you join our team?

132
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:45,350
I'll join.

133
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:49,490
I transferred to Nankatsu. We'll play soccer together!

134
00:07:51,490 --> 00:07:52,500
Hooray!

135
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,340
You're really good at soccer.

136
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,590
That shot earlier really impressed me.

137
00:07:56,590 --> 00:07:58,590
Didn't I tell you? Didn't I?

138
00:07:58,590 --> 00:08:02,940
Plus, a former Brazilian soccer player is going to coach us!

139
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,000
Isn't that great?!

140
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,250
Let the new Nankatsu team's training begin!

141
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,010
Yes!

142
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,070
Genzo.

143
00:08:16,070 --> 00:08:18,430
Are your wounds okay?

144
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:21,050
You need to rest today.

145
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,020
I lost.

146
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,290
Against Ozora Tsubasa.

147
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:36,950
Maybe the fact that I didn't concede a goal in the national tournament made me arrogant.

148
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:38,910
Don't dwell on it so much.

149
00:08:38,910 --> 00:08:40,720
How could I not?!

150
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:44,940
If I can't stop his shots...

151
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:47,800
...becoming champion last year means nothing.

152
00:08:56,670 --> 00:09:00,060
Let's start with running. Then we'll do passing drills.

153
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,770
Let's go!

154
00:09:07,730 --> 00:09:10,650
Tsubasa, will you be my partner for passing?

155
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:11,330
Yes.

156
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:29,860
Look, Tsubasa.

157
00:09:30,850 --> 00:09:34,840
It was bothering me, so I looked into it...

158
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:37,050
...even though you're really good at soccer...

159
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:40,390
...you've never participated in a national soccer tournament.

160
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:43,030
Didn't your old school have a soccer club?

161
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,140
It did, but...

162
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,550
...they weren't that good.

163
00:09:48,550 --> 00:09:50,150
Even with you there?!

164
00:09:51,650 --> 00:09:54,650
No one liked soccer.

165
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:57,200
All some of them cared about was shooting.

166
00:09:57,720 --> 00:10:00,840
They also quit because they found the practices too tough.

167
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,870
There are people like that everywhere.

168
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:05,140
Everyone wants to be a forward.

169
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:07,320
But not everyone can score goals.

170
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,710
They find that boring too.

171
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:12,890
Isn't that why we're practicing though?

172
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:14,960
After all...

173
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:19,150
...all of us here love soccer, right?

174
00:10:19,150 --> 00:10:20,840
Yes, exactly.

175
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,850
Of course we love it.

176
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:27,460
Otherwise, we wouldn't put up with getting beaten by Shutetsu every year, right?

177
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:31,770
Someone's coming.

178
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:39,490
What are you doing here?!

179
00:10:45,970 --> 00:10:51,060
Translation: ARE-YOU-SURE
www.areyousuresubs.com

180
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,050
Hey, Ishizaki.

181
00:10:56,050 --> 00:10:57,530
Urabe!

182
00:10:58,220 --> 00:10:59,480
What team is this?

183
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:01,720
The Nishigaoka Elementary soccer team.

184
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,030
A school from the next town.

185
00:11:04,230 --> 00:11:06,110
They're a pretty strong team.

186
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,870
We came just like we promised.

187
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:11,000
What promise are you talking about?

188
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:13,030
What are you talking about?

189
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:16,420
You're the one who suggested the practice match!

190
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,390
Ha?!

191
00:11:20,110 --> 00:11:20,910
Roberto!

192
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,390
Actually, it was me who suggested it.

193
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:27,030
You finally made it, Coach! You're really late!

194
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:31,110
- What? Roberto Hongo?
- Yes.

195
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:33,720
But this guy drinks alcohol...

196
00:11:33,870 --> 00:11:35,510
Is it really him?

197
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:37,870
Of course it is! Don't you know?

198
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:41,750
It was all over the news that a great player came to Japan!

199
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:42,950
Really?

200
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:46,950
Is this okay? He's drinking alcohol even though it's not even afternoon yet.

201
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,080
He's not your typical drunk!

202
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:50,870
He's truly a great person.

203
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:54,720
Was this the present you mentioned this morning?

204
00:11:54,870 --> 00:11:55,320
Yes.

205
00:11:55,510 --> 00:11:57,750
What a lousy soccer team this is.

206
00:11:57,910 --> 00:11:58,910
What?!

207
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,510
Your coach is a drunkard.

208
00:12:01,670 --> 00:12:02,720
Roberto--

209
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,270
No, he's really good.

210
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:13,420
Though he does look a bit different from his playing days.

211
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,550
Are you making fun of us?

212
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:18,510
All eyes were on him, but then he suddenly disappeared.

213
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:20,110
Guys, I'm counting on you!

214
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:22,840
Maybe it's because of the alcohol?

215
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,910
Could be.

216
00:12:25,790 --> 00:12:28,000
You guys picked a pretty weird coach.

217
00:12:28,950 --> 00:12:31,360
Against Shutetsu...

218
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:33,670
...no wonder you lost 30-0!

219
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,510
30-0?!

220
00:12:39,270 --> 00:12:42,510
If we're aiming to beat Shutetsu...

221
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:45,390
...we need to create a similar goal difference too.

222
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,110
Well said.

223
00:12:47,270 --> 00:12:51,080
That kid... He just says whatever comes to mind!

224
00:12:51,230 --> 00:12:52,910
Is 30-0 true?

225
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,630
Well... Yes.

226
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:58,670
Tsubasa! I'm counting on you to thrash them!

227
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,360
Okay.

228
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:01,470
Let's begin, then.

229
00:13:01,630 --> 00:13:03,670
If we don't hurry, it'll get dark.

230
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:06,420
What are you talking about?! It's just past noon, you idiot!

231
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:19,270
Maybe I need to act like a coach.

232
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:21,840
Then start with that alcohol!

233
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,200
It's forbidden here!

234
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,510
I understand.

235
00:13:27,910 --> 00:13:31,270
You need to throw that in the trash!

236
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:34,230
But I just bought it, wouldn't that be a waste?

237
00:13:35,870 --> 00:13:37,870
It's not a great thing off the field either!

238
00:13:38,030 --> 00:13:39,030
Calm down, calm down.

239
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:42,270
By the way, everyone, who is your captain?

240
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,720
I am.

241
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:46,320
What? You are?

242
00:13:46,470 --> 00:13:47,630
We hadn't decided yet.

243
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:50,950
What are you saying?! It's always been me!

244
00:13:51,230 --> 00:13:55,470
Then Ishizaki, raise your voice and guide everyone.

245
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:56,950
Alright, got it!

246
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,870
You already do that all the time.

247
00:13:59,030 --> 00:14:00,720
All you ever say is "run."

248
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:01,910
So what?

249
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:03,470
That's good too.

250
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:04,910
Hearing the captain's voice...

251
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:06,670
...gives everyone strength.

252
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:07,630
Yes.

253
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:10,200
Roberto, any other advice?

254
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,750
Let me think...

255
00:14:14,110 --> 00:14:15,110
I guess not.

256
00:14:16,270 --> 00:14:18,910
First, let me see everyone's level.

257
00:14:19,230 --> 00:14:21,110
This match is perfect for that.

258
00:14:22,110 --> 00:14:24,600
I'll decide what position you'll play.

259
00:14:25,110 --> 00:14:27,360
Play with all your strength.

260
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,470
Okay!

261
00:14:30,630 --> 00:14:31,360
Tsubasa!

262
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:32,910
What is it, Roberto?

263
00:14:33,390 --> 00:14:34,320
Don't forget.

264
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:36,600
The ball is your friend.

265
00:14:40,270 --> 00:14:41,910
The ball is waiting...

266
00:14:42,470 --> 00:14:43,720
...to play with you.

267
00:14:47,110 --> 00:14:48,550
Alright, go on now!

268
00:14:49,510 --> 00:14:50,510
Yes, sir!

269
00:15:04,630 --> 00:15:06,750
Referee, sir, I'm counting on you.

270
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,230
Thanks.

271
00:15:15,150 --> 00:15:19,550
So the friendly match between Nishigaoka and Nankatsu is about to begin.

272
00:15:20,230 --> 00:15:21,360
20 minutes per half.

273
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:23,840
Nishigaoka will kick off.

274
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:34,200
Who is that? I didn't know Nankatsu had someone like that.

275
00:15:35,110 --> 00:15:38,420
Whatever. What difference does it make?

276
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:43,720
Alright, let's start by scoring 30 goals!

277
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:44,600
Okay!

278
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,000
They're messing around!

279
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:49,750
What?!

280
00:15:51,670 --> 00:15:52,600
Nice pass!

281
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,080
What happened? What happened?

282
00:16:00,110 --> 00:16:01,870
Guys, stop them!

283
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:13,360
Urabe!

284
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,200
Nice tackle.

285
00:16:20,790 --> 00:16:23,150
Nishigaoka's captain...

286
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:26,270
...you cannot stop Urabe Hanji-sama!

287
00:16:29,390 --> 00:16:30,230
What?!

288
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:31,910
- What?!
- No way!

289
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:33,720
Well done, Tsubasa!

290
00:16:33,950 --> 00:16:35,000
Great!

291
00:16:37,670 --> 00:16:38,720
Go!

292
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,550
Tsubasa, what are you doing?!

293
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:46,840
That's our goal!

294
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,550
Tsubasa!

295
00:16:56,550 --> 00:16:57,390
Let's go!

296
00:17:04,590 --> 00:17:05,230
I'm going to shoot!

297
00:17:20,230 --> 00:17:22,000
- It went in.
- Seriously?

298
00:17:26,070 --> 00:17:27,750
You did it, Tsubasa!

299
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,750
I've never seen anything like it!

300
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:32,270
What a blast!

301
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:34,860
We did it, guys.

302
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:37,550
Amazing! He shot from so far away!

303
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,350
We did it, we did it, we did it!

304
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:42,070
What is this guy?

305
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:43,590
A guy like that...

306
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:45,860
...was playing at Nankatsu?

307
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,550
Come on, let's answer back!

308
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,830
# NANKATSU : 2
NISHIGAOKA : 0 #

309
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:05,160
We can still turn this around, even after two goals!

310
